{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Shifrah</b> — twice in the Masorah with two readings. This one and the other: ברוחו שמים שפרה. For the way of midwives: sometimes when the infant is formed dead, the midwife takes a reed tube and places it inside the child's intestines and blows into it and restores breath to the child — and this is שפרה, in the sense of שפופרת. Another interpretation: why is her name called Shifrah? Because she beautifies (משפרת) the infant. Also ברוחו שמים שפרה — on account of that HaShem beautified (שפר) the heavens."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:36.850170486Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}